*HOST:* The controversial social media influencer Andrew Tate has been arrested in Romania on suspicion of human trafficking, rape, and forming an organized crime group. Our correspondent Ashna Hernag is here with more. For the uninitiated, who is he and what is he being accused of in more detail?

*ASHNA HERNAG:* Well, Andrew Tate is a former kickboxer, but as you mentioned there, he is a deeply controversial online influencer. He first rose to prominence after an appearance on UK reality show Big Brother back in 2016. He has gained a huge following in recent years, particularly among teenage boys and young men. His content often promotes a hyper-masculine lifestyle and denigrates women. He has been accused of misogyny.

More recently, he has been banned from multiple social media platforms. His accounts have been removed from TikTok, Instagram, YouTube, and Facebook. He has now been arrested in Romania on charges that include human trafficking and rape. Prosecutors allege that he and his brother, along with two other suspects, recruited women through false pretenses of love and then subjected them to physical violence and sexual assault. They have been detained for 24 hours, with prosecutors expected to apply for a 30-day extension. Tate has denied the allegations through his lawyer, who claims the arrest is politically motivated.

The case is particularly significant given his influence on young people. Experts say his content can have a negative impact on how young men view women and relationships, highlighting the wider social concerns about manosphere influencers.
